.TH HTTP_REQUEST_NEW 3
.SH NAME
http_request_new \- create a request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "http_request* http_request_new(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_request_new ()
allocates a request (type GET, empty location, headers and body) and puts it on top of
.IR h->request ;
the one that was there becomes
.IR next .
Headers and body functions work on this request.
.BR http_open (3)
calls it and sets the type.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The request, or 0 if the memory is short.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_open(3), http_response_new(3), http_free(3)
